{"id": "9e0c193c-67f7-4733-be72-c8430c952e92", "slug": "airspace-monitor-1", "title": "Airspace Monitor", "description": "Airspace Monitor Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-top-creators-featured\"\nname: \"Airspace Monitor\"\ndescription: \"Airspace Monitor Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#FF0000\"\n  secondary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  accent: \"#FF0000\"\n  background: \"#050505\"\n  surface: \"#E6DCD2\"\n  text-primary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-secondary: \"#A1A1AA\"\n  border: \"#50463C\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"8px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# Airspace Monitor\nSource: Neuform Featured templates from top creators. Author: Meng To (@mengto). Views: 6; favorites: 13; remixes: 0.\nTags: background, animated, webgl, effect.\n## Overview\nAirspace Monitor Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.\n\nT-14:00 TRACKING TARGET\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: TRACKING TARGET.\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #FF0000, secondary #FFFFFF, accent #FF0000, background #050505, surface #E6DCD2, text-primary #FFFFFF. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Inter for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nCards, buttons, badges, navigation, and repeated blocks should preserve the source geometry, border treatment, and hover feel.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\" class=\"antialiased bg-[#020202] text-white selection:bg-neutral-800 selection:text-white\"><head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Airspace Monitor</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/ScrollTrigger.min.js\"></script>\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin=\"\">\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;600&amp;display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n</head>\n<body class=\"relative min-h-screen w-full bg-[#050505] text-white overflow-hidden font-['Inter',sans-serif]\" style=\"background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, transparent, transparent 1px, rgba(255,255,255,0.015) 1px, rgba(255,255,255,0.015) 8px);\">\n\n    <!-- Skill: Framed Grid Layout & Beautiful Shadows -->\n    <div id=\"border-frame\" class=\"absolute inset-[1.5rem] md:inset-[3rem] pointer-events-none z-0 shadow-[0_2.8px_2.2px_rgba(0,_0,_0,_0.034),_0_6.7px_5.3px_rgba(0,_0,_0,_0.048),_0_12.5px_10px_rgba(0,_0,_0,_0.06),_0_22.3px_17.9px_rgba(0,_0,_0,_0.072),_0_41.8px_33.4px_rgba(0,_0,_0,_0.086),_0_100px_80px_rgba(0,_0,_0,_0.12)]\">\n\n        <!-- Primary boundary lines (dimmer, spanning full width/height) -->\n        <div class=\"absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-[1px] bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-neutral-700/30 to-transparent\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute bottom-0 left-0 w-full h-[1px] bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-neutral-700/30 to-transparent\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute top-0 left-0 w-[1px] h-full bg-gradient-to-b from-transparent via-neutral-700/30 to-transparent\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute top-0 right-0 w-[1px] h-full bg-gradient-to-b from-transparent via-neutral-700/30 to-transparent\"></div>\n\n        <!-- Secondary hierarchy: Inner crosshairs (very subtle) -->\n        <div class=\"absolute top-1/2 left-[5%] w-[90%] h-[1px] bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-neutral-800/40 to-transparent -translate-y-1/2\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute top-[5%] left-1/2 w-[1px] h-[90%] bg-gradient-to-b from-transparent via-neutral-800/40 to-transparent -translate-x-1/2\"></div>\n\n        <!-- Tertiary hierarchy: Corner L-Brackets (thicker and brighter) -->\n        <div class=\"absolute top-0 left-0 w-6 h-6 border-t-2 border-l-2 border-neutral-400/80\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute top-0 right-0 w-6 h-6 border-t-2 border-r-2 border-neutral-400/80\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute bottom-0 left-0 w-6 h-6 border-b-2 border-l-2 border-neutral-400/80\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute bottom-0 right-0 w-6 h-6 border-b-2 border-r-2 border-neutral-400/80\"></div>\n\n        <!-- Flashlight Hover Effect on Borders -->\n        <div class=\"pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 transition-opacity duration-300 z-10\" style=\"opacity: var(--flash-opacity, 0);\">\n            <div class=\"absolute inset-0 border border-white/80\" style=\"-webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(250px circle at var(--mouse-x, 0) var(--mouse-y, 0), black, transparent); mask-image: radial-gradient(250px circle at var(--mouse-x, 0) var(--mouse-y, 0), black, transparent);\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Skill: Border Gradients (Inner Box Reveal) -->\n        <div class=\"absolute inset-0 border border-transparent\" style=\"background: linear-gradient(to bottom right, rgba(255,255,255,0.06), rgba(255,255,255,0)) border-box; -webkit-mask: linear-gradient(#fff 0 0) padding-box, linear-gradient(#fff 0 0); -webkit-mask-composite: destination-out; mask-composite: exclude;\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- UI Overlay Layer -->\n    <div class=\"absolute inset-0 z-20 pointer-events-none flex flex-col justify-between p-8 md:p-16\">\n        <!-- Timer Top Right -->\n        <div class=\"flex justify-end w-full\">\n            <div class=\"font-semibold text-[3rem] md:text-[5rem] tracking-tighter text-white leading-none drop-shadow-lg font-sans\">T-14:00</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Skill: Masked Reveal Text -->\n        <div class=\"absolute left-1/2 top-[65%] -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-full text-center mix-blend-screen\">\n            <h1 class=\"flex justify-center gap-3 md:gap-6 text-[14vw] md:text-[9vw] font-semibold tracking-tighter leading-none whitespace-nowrap\">\n                <div class=\"overflow-hidden pb-[0.2rem] -mb-[0.2rem]\">\n                    <span class=\"inline-block reveal-text text-white drop-shadow-xl font-sans font-light\">TRACKING</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"overflow-hidden pb-[0.2rem] -mb-[0.2rem]\">\n                    <span class=\"inline-block reveal-text text-neutral-400 drop-shadow-xl font-sans font-light\">TARGET</span>\n                </div>\n            </h1>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- WebGL-style Canvas Animation Layer -->\n    <div class=\"absolute inset-0 z-10 flex items-center justify-center pointer-events-none\">\n        <canvas id=\"radarCanvas\" class=\"w-full h-full mix-blend-lighten\"></canvas>\n    </div>\n\n    <script>\n        // Flashlight Hover Effect Tracking\n        document.addEventListener(\"mousemove\", (e) => {\n            const frame = document.getElementById(\"border-frame\");\n            if (!frame) return;\n            const rect = frame.getBoundingClientRect();\n\n            const isHovered = e.clientX >= rect.left && e.clientX <= rect.right &&\n                              e.clientY >= rect.top && e.clientY <= rect.bottom;\n\n            const x = e.clientX - rect.left;\n            const y = e.clientY - rect.top;\n\n            frame.style.setProperty('--mouse-x', `${x}px`);\n            frame.style.setProperty('--mouse-y', `${y}px`);\n            frame.style.setProperty('--flash-opacity', isHovered ? '1' : '0');\n        });\n\n        // GSAP Masked Reveal Animation\n        document.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n            gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);\n\n            gsap.set(\".reveal-text\", { y: \"110%\" });\n\n            gsap.to(\".reveal-text\", {\n                y: \"0%\",\n                duration: 1.4,\n                stagger: 0.15,\n                ease: \"power4.out\",\n                delay: 0.3\n            });\n        });\n\n        // Procedural Radar Animation (WebGL alternative for single file)\n        const canvas = document.getElementById('radarCanvas');\n        const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n        let width, height, cx, cy, maxRadius;\n        let angle = 0;\n\n        function resizeCanvas() {\n            const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n            width = window.innerWidth;\n            height = window.innerHeight;\n            canvas.width = width * dpr;\n            canvas.height = height * dpr;\n            ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);\n\n            cx = width / 2;\n            cy = height / 2;\n            // Match the visual scale of the reference image\n            maxRadius = Math.min(width, height) * 0.42;\n        }\n\n        window.addEventListener('resize', resizeCanvas);\n        resizeCanvas();\n\n        function drawRadar() {\n            ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);\n\n            // 1. Center Ambient Glow\n            const bgGrad = ctx.createRadialGradient(cx, cy, 0, cx, cy, maxRadius);\n            bgGrad.addColorStop(0, 'rgba(230, 220, 210, 0.25)'); // Bright warm center\n            bgGrad.addColorStop(0.3, 'rgba(80, 70, 60, 0.15)');\n            bgGrad.addColorStop(0.8, 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)');\n            ctx.fillStyle = bgGrad;\n            ctx.beginPath();\n            ctx.arc(cx, cy, maxRadius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\n            ctx.fill();\n\n            // 2. Concentric Grid Rings\n            ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35)';\n            ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n            const rings = [0.35, 0.65, 1];\n            rings.forEach(scale => {\n                ctx.beginPath();\n                ctx.arc(cx, cy, maxRadius * scale, 0, Math.PI * 2);\n                ctx.stroke();\n            });\n\n            // 3. Crosshairs\n            ctx.beginPath();\n            const ext = 30; // Extend slightly past max radius\n            ctx.moveTo(cx, cy - maxRadius - ext);\n            ctx.lineTo(cx, cy + maxRadius + ext);\n            ctx.moveTo(cx - maxRadius - ext, cy);\n            ctx.lineTo(cx + maxRadius + ext, cy);\n            ctx.stroke();\n\n            // 4. Tick Marks and Degree Labels\n            ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6)';\n            ctx.font = '10px Inter, sans-serif';\n            ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n            ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';\n\n            for(let i = 0; i < 360; i += 2) {\n                // Orient 0 degrees to the top, move clockwise\n                const angleRad = (i - 90) * (Math.PI / 180);\n                const isMajor = i % 20 === 0;\n                const isMedium = i % 10 === 0;\n\n                let tickLength = 4;\n                if (isMajor) tickLength = 12;\n                else if (isMedium) tickLength = 8;\n\n                const startR = maxRadius;\n                const endR = maxRadius - tickLength;\n\n                ctx.beginPath();\n                ctx.moveTo(cx + Math.cos(angleRad) * startR, cy + Math.sin(angleRad) * startR);\n                ctx.lineTo(cx + Math.cos(angleRad) * endR, cy + Math.sin(angleRad) * endR);\n                ctx.strokeStyle = isMajor ? 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8)' : 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3)';\n                ctx.stroke();\n\n                if (isMajor) {\n                    const textOffset = maxRadius + 18;\n                    const tx = cx + Math.cos(angleRad) * textOffset;\n                    const ty = cy + Math.sin(angleRad) * textOffset;\n\n                    ctx.save();\n                    ctx.translate(tx, ty);\n                    // Orient text inwards towards center\n                    ctx.rotate(angleRad + Math.PI/2);\n                    ctx.fillText(i.toString(), 0, 0);\n                    ctx.restore();\n                }\n            }\n\n            // 5. Sweeping Radar Beam\n            ctx.save();\n            ctx.translate(cx, cy);\n            ctx.rotate(angle);\n\n            if (ctx.createConicGradient) {\n                const sweepGrad = ctx.createConicGradient(0, 0, 0);\n                // Draw a fading tail counter-clockwise from 0 (leading edge)\n                sweepGrad.addColorStop(0, 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0)');\n                sweepGrad.addColorStop(0.85, 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0)');\n                sweepGrad.addColorStop(0.98, 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15)');\n                sweepGrad.addColorStop(1, 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7)');\n\n                ctx.fillStyle = sweepGrad;\n                ctx.beginPath();\n                ctx.moveTo(0,0);\n                ctx.arc(0, 0, maxRadius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\n                ctx.fill();\n\n                // Bright leading edge line\n                ctx.beginPath();\n                ctx.moveTo(0,0);\n                ctx.lineTo(maxRadius, 0);\n                ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95)';\n                ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;\n                ctx.stroke();\n            }\n            ctx.restore();\n\n            // 6. Target Dot\n            // Position fixed at roughly top-right quadrant\n            const dotAngle = -Math.PI / 4 + 0.12;\n            const dotDist = maxRadius * 0.55;\n            const targetX = cx + Math.cos(dotAngle) * dotDist;\n            const targetY = cy + Math.sin(dotAngle) * dotDist;\n\n            ctx.beginPath();\n            ctx.arc(targetX, targetY, 9, 0, Math.PI*2);\n            ctx.fillStyle = '#ff0000'; // Pure red\n            ctx.fill();\n\n            // Increment sweep rotation\n            angle += 0.015;\n            requestAnimationFrame(drawRadar);\n        }\n\n        requestAnimationFrame(drawRadar);\n    </script>\n\n</body></html>", "preview_file_name": "airspace-monitor-1.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/regenerated-2026-05-22-2s/airspace-monitor-1.jpg", "source_name": "airspace-monitor-1-DESIGN.md", "views": 48, "forks": 1, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "9109ecbb-cdc4-4815-981e-2ea83be13765", "created_at": "2026-05-01T16:18:09.070118+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-06-30T09:53:16.88842+00:00"}